    "text": "Three local scroll sketches are ready. **I recommend A**, because the fixture comes from work you personally built.\n\n| Concept | Story and object | Preview |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A · At the fixture** | A bench checklist carried by solid fixture modules; follows firmware decisions into physical observation. | [Open A](http://127.0.0.1:3000/sketch/fixture) |\n| **B · Power-state selector** | A state-table story carried by a teaching selector; distinguishes scheduling from observed behavior. | [Open B](http://127.0.0.1:3000/sketch/states) |\n| **C · Observation lead** | A timing-diagram reading carried by a segmented bench lead; emphasizes what the evidence supports. | [Open C](http://127.0.0.1:3000/sketch/lead) |\n\nAll three use explanatory geometry and confirmed facts. Desktop and phone checks passed; styling is provisional. Nothing is published.\n\n**Which concept should carry your portfolio: A, B or C?** Your selection leads to the full storyboard, including the Mosslink page and corrected HTML CV.\n\nThe [storyfolio skill](.agents/skills/storyfolio/SKILL.md) requires proceeding when “They have picked one, or told you to pick.” I’m pausing here for that design choice.",
