    {
      "command": "/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> docs/story/facts.md <<'EOF'\n\n## User-confirmed corrections and scope (12 October 2026)\n\nThese answers supersede conflicting résumé wording. Source: user's second message.\n\n- Use Ada Mensah and Mosslink publicly. Exclude employer and employment dates from site and downloadable CV; current employment details not confirmed. Do not imply a formal current title.\n- Ada wrote firmware, scheduled power states and built the bring-up fixture. Colleague designed PCB and analogue front end. Do not claim Ada owned complete sensor or hardware design.\n- Two-year figure is a projection from bench currents and an assumed reporting cycle; longest run 72 hours. No field endurance or weather testing supports two-year claim. Reporting interval and calculation attribution remain unconfirmed; omit them.\n- Forty engineering samples assembled, six tested on bench, none to customers. No field pilot or product launch. Do not claim Ada personally assembled/tested all units.\n- One preliminary emissions check passed; full qualification unfinished. Never certified or qualified.\n- Radio-awake problem was seen in a current trace after failed transmission. Cause, fix, timing and later resolution unconfirmed; all excluded. No trace available.\n- Own fixture photograph and simplified power-state diagram have public-use permission. Photograph remains unavailable. Colleague circuit diagram has no permission and is excluded.\n- Supplied SVGs may stand in as labelled explanations only. Neither is photograph, original wiring, firmware, current trace or test result. Sleep/Measure/Transmit is a teaching sequence with no durations/current values.\n- Audience: firmware hiring manager. Purpose: understand how Ada connects code to measurable signal.\n- Working documents: state table, timing diagram, current trace. Bring-up means checking new board's basic operation. Prior notes also establish bench checklists.\n- Lesson in user's words: a firmware decision needs a physical observation; estimate and observed run support different claims. No implication every issue resolved or every device tested.\n- Public example email: ada@example.com, link only. Do not send email or claim tested delivery.\n- Make corrected printable HTML CV downloadable; no invented PDF. No old site or testimonials.\n- Mosslink only project; include dedicated project page and main-story appearance. No invented project, photograph, testimonial, award or result.\n- English; ordinary navigation; share preview; site icon; useful missing-page page. No blog/chat/translation/form. Legal/jurisdiction deferred to publishing; no compliance claim.\n- Local system fonts, supplied local drawings or original explanatory geometry only. No external purchase/download. No additional skills installed; user declined.\n- Unconfirmed facts stay out. Employer/dates and unavailable artifacts are excluded, not blockers.\n\n## Remaining unanswered facts\n\n- Reporting interval, model author, cause/fix/resolution of radio issue, exact individual test/assembly scope and current formal employment details. None may be inferred or used.\n- Public use of employer-specific hardware detail is not established: use generic explanatory geometry, never a reconstruction.\nEOF\nnode .agents/skills/storyfolio/scripts/scaffold.mjs site\"",
